VoltOS is free software. The installed system is made of many programs,
each under its own licence; the licence of every package is in
/usr/share/licenses on the installed system.

The main parts:

  - VoltOS's own packages and scripts: MIT licence.
  - The Linux kernel: GNU General Public License, version 2.
  - OpenZFS: Common Development and Distribution License (CDDL) 1.0.
  - ZFSBootMenu: MIT licence.
  - The MATE desktop, GNOME Flashback and most applications: GNU General
    Public License and GNU Lesser General Public License.
  - This installer: based on the OpenSolaris installer (Caiman) from Sun
    Microsystems and Oracle, CDDL 1.0, with VoltOS's changes under the MIT
    licence.

